  --summary "A gate that cannot look does not guess. running_gates(namespace).unwrap_or(0) turned every failure to read the cluster into zero — the exact value that satisfies the guard two lines below it, if shared && running > 0. No KUBECONFIG, an unreachable API server, or a credential that may create Jobs but not list pods all read as healthy and idle, so the guard protecting against two gates crossing receipts on one shared disk failed OPEN. On a SHARED workspace an unreadable count now refuses and carries the diagnostic running_gates already writes; on a private workspace it still degrades to zero, where the count only drives an advisory crowding notice." \
  --excludes "Does NOT make the count readable — supplying KUBECONFIG is the operator's job and this only stops the guard from guessing when it is absent. Does NOT change the private-workspace path: refusing there would turn a missing hint into a blocked gate, which is why the fix is conditional on `shared` rather than a blanket propagate. Does NOT document the environment a hand-run gate needs (KUBECONFIG + BOSS_JOBS_URL); that is a CLAUDE.md doors change and belongs in its own car. Does NOT touch running_gates itself — its diagnostic was already correct and was simply being discarded." \
  --test "Three unit tests over a pure resolve_running(shared, Result): a shared workspace refuses on an unreadable count AND the refusal preserves the underlying KUBECONFIG diagnostic (discarding it is what sent an operator to a raw kubectl openapi error from the later create); a private workspace degrades to zero; and readable counts pass through both ways INCLUDING a successful read of zero, so the fix cannot turn a genuinely idle cluster into a refusal. 25 gate:: tests pass, clippy -D warnings clean." \
